        "id": "e1f2a3b4c5d60001",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "Shared state: logical state",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "Use the inject buttons to set the physical states `exampleMotion` and `exampleDoorOpen`.\nWhenever one of them changes, a function node reads both from the global context and derives the logical state `examplePersonInRoom`. The rule is deliberately simple: a person is in the room if motion is detected while the door is closed. The get-shared-state node sends `examplePersonInRoom` to the debug sidebar when it changes.\n\nPersist is set to Off, so nothing is written to disk."
